The text leading up to this was:
--------------------------
|# Redoubt no-webcompat-reporter.patch (Android, LW-M7-38): no "Report broken
|# site" menu entry.
|#
|# Upstream files touched
|# -----------------------
|#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/MoreSettingsSubmenu.kt
|#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt
|#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilderTest.kt
|#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/MoreSettingsSubmenuTest.kt
|#
|# Line numbers are from the Firefox 158.0 tree; no other listed patch edits
|# these files.
|#
|# Why
|# ---
|# LibreWolf's policies.json sets DisableFeedbackCommands, which removes the
|# product feedback commands, "Report broken site" among them. Fenix 158 has the
|# entry in the main menu's "More" submenu. What it does in Redoubt:
|#   * with Settings.isTelemetryEnabled true (Fenix's default; Redoubt does not
|#     change it), it opens the WebCompatReporter form, whose Send submits
|#     Gecko's broken-site-report Glean ping. Redoubt has no Glean upload path
|#     (no-glean.patch, disable-data-reporting-common.patch), so the report is
|#     silently discarded while the UI says it was sent;
|#   * with it false, MenuNavigationMiddleware skips the form and opens
|#     https://webcompat.com/issues/new?url=<page address> in a new tab,
|#     handing the page address and the page's web-compat details to a third
|#     party.
|#
|# What it does
|# ------------
|# Removes the entry from both menus that offer it:
|#   * MoreSettingsSubmenu (the menu every user sees,
|#     MenuDialogFragment): the WebCompatReporterMenuItem call and the private
|#     composable. The isWebCompatEnabled / onWebCompatReporterClick parameters
|#     stay, so MenuDialogFragment.kt (also edited by delete-on-quit-swipe.patch)
|#     is not touched; they are now unused.
|#   * BrowserMenuBuilder's default configuration (the customizable menu
|#     behind Settings.isMenuCustomizationEnabled, off by default): the
|#     ReportBrokenSite item of "More".
|# Unchanged: the reporter code, its navigation targets (unreachable without
|# the entry), and android-components' WebCompatFeature, which installs the
|# webcompat@mozilla.org site interventions that keep broken sites working and
|# reports nothing.
|#
|# Tests: BrowserMenuBuilderTest asserts no default layout (toolbar top/bottom,
|# expanded or not) contains ReportBrokenSite; MoreSettingsSubmenuTest asserts
|# the entry does not render even with isWebCompatEnabled = true. The
|# instrumented ThreeDotMenuMainRobot / MainMenuTest still look for the entry;
|# they are not part of the unit gate.
|#
|diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt
|index 38153c1..b914c23 100644
|--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt
|+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt
